If they're still alive after that,

265
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:42,040
I'm afraid Lady Luck
just isn't on our side.

266
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:46,752
But if we can't sink them
today, we'll sink them tomorrow.

267
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:56,800
Hey, that's one of our ships.

268
00:18:57,020 --> 00:18:58,902
Why is it taking off on its own?

269
00:18:59,700 --> 00:19:01,000
Hurry up, damn it!

270
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,080
Follow that submarine!

271
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:06,177
Okay, but I mean, it's already underwater.

272
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:09,677
Also, I'm pretty sure everyone on it is
dead after those attacks from the Admiral.

273
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:10,590
Sorry!

274
00:19:10,673 --> 00:19:11,503
They're alive.

275
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:13,220
I'm certain of it.

276
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:20,840
With my authority as a warlord of the sea,

277
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:23,720
I shall pursue and
capture Straw Hat Luffy,

278
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:25,480
no matter the cost!

279
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:26,820
Yes, help!

280
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:29,960
That's great, but, like, how?

281
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:31,860
Just shut up and go!

282
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:34,010
Whoa!

283
00:19:34,093 --> 00:19:36,160
It's so hot when she yells at us!

284
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:42,120
You scum-sucking red-haired
sack of excrement!

285
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:46,100
You're telling me the
treasure map thing was a lie?

286
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:51,697
Just having some fun, old friend?

287
00:19:51,780 --> 00:19:53,777
It's been a while, huh?

288
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:56,457
Screw you!

289
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:58,160
It's been a while, huh?

290
00:19:59,940 --> 00:20:03,197
What did you think that I'd forgive
you for what you did out of kindness?

291
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:04,577
That I'd forget?

292
00:20:04,660 --> 00:20:06,717
Forget about what?

293
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:08,817
Don't give me that!

294
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:11,397
If you hadn't snuck up on me back then,

295
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:14,397
I never would have eaten that
Devil Fruit and more importantly,

296
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:16,337
I never would have lost that treasure map.

297
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,677
In other words, I'd?

298
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:20,584
Be filthy rich instead
of running from the Navy.

299
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:24,920
Oh, is that so?

300
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:27,600
Playing it cool.

301
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:29,056
I should have known.

302
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:33,652
All these years and you're still a
prodigy when it comes to pissing me off.

303
00:20:33,780 --> 00:20:37,777
You've hardly been here five minutes
and you've already lied and cheated me.

304
00:20:37,860 --> 00:20:39,797
You said you were going to stop the war.

305
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:43,620
Well, you're about to start
a new one with me right now.

306
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:45,760
Once a chump, always a chump.

307
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:48,080
You see that?

308
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:49,730
Sure did.

309
00:20:49,813 --> 00:20:53,077
Even the emperors can't
escape his trash talk!

310
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,740
He's such a pro.

311
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:02,240
Captain Back, could you be more perfect?

312
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:05,029
We will follow you to
the end of the world.

313
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:08,300
I really did miss you though?

314
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:11,140
Oh, I'm sure you did.

315
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:17,080
But wait, these guys
are certified badasses.

316
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:22,386
If I can catch a ride with my old Gourmet,
I can get off this island scot-free.

317
00:21:27,820 --> 00:21:28,720
What now?

318
00:21:31,980 --> 00:21:35,057
Marco, there's nothing to
gain from fighting anymore.

319
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:37,320
Just walk away nice and easy.

320
00:21:42,340 --> 00:21:43,170
Hawkeye!

321
00:21:43,280 --> 00:21:44,300
Get back here!

322
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:50,081
I agreed to fight Whitebeard
and his allies, true.

323
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:52,720
But red hair is another matter entirely.

324
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:57,120
You should quit as well.

325
00:21:59,140 --> 00:22:01,434
Your thirst for battle is your undoing.

326
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:06,900
Every blow you land upon your
enemies, you land upon your own men.

327
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:13,140
However if anyone here
still hungers for battle

328
00:22:16,860 --> 00:22:23,140
Fine then come we shall be
more than happy to face you

329
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:46,520
Well teach you want to
try sorry Blackbeard

330
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:53,397
Pretty as a picture
aren't you i got what i

331
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:55,977
came for here after all
and i'm not looking for

332
00:22:56,060 --> 00:22:59,117
a fight With you guys
well not yet at least

333
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:04,220
come on fellas let's pack
it up Zia-ha-ha-ha-ha!

334
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:19,660
I don't know.

335
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:45,900
Accept your losses.

336
00:23:48,640 --> 00:23:50,180
Honor the fallen.

337
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:53,777
Withdraw from battle.

338
00:23:53,860 --> 00:23:55,331
With your dignity intact.

339
00:24:10,480 --> 00:24:13,280
Thank you.

340
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:40,160
I think it's finally over now.

341
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:43,980
As for Whitebeard and Ace,

342
00:24:44,920 --> 00:24:48,979
I'm sure you won't object to their
friends taking care of the burial.

343
00:24:51,100 --> 00:24:54,500
The battle was already
broadcast to the entire world.

344
00:24:55,120 --> 00:24:57,717
I won't allow you to make a
further spectacle of their

345
00:24:57,800 --> 00:25:00,976
deaths by parading their
corpses around like trophies.

346
00:25:01,160 --> 00:25:02,680
And why shouldn't we?

347
00:25:02,860 --> 00:25:05,097
If they wanted a proper burial so badly,

348
00:25:05,180 --> 00:25:07,537
that perhaps they shouldn't
have defied the navy.

349
00:25:07,620 --> 00:25:09,937
We have every right to
string the bastards up.

350
00:25:10,020 --> 00:25:12,037
And why should we listen
to a pirate anyway?

351
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:13,120
It's our victory.

352
00:25:13,300 --> 00:25:14,240
We earned it.

353
00:25:14,460 --> 00:25:15,460
That's enough.

354
00:25:17,460 --> 00:25:18,480
But, sir!

355
00:25:22,800 --> 00:25:24,600
I'll allow it, Shanks.

356
00:25:24,980 --> 00:25:27,360
Just this once. But why?

357
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:30,200
Let me take responsibility.

358
00:25:33,820 --> 00:25:34,740
Thank you.

359
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:38,066
Now go treat the injured
before it's too late.

360
00:25:44,760 --> 00:25:46,300
This war is over.

361
00:25:47,380 --> 00:25:49,360
That Navy has won.

362
00:25:57,200 --> 00:25:59,480
If you can help the medics, hop to it.

363
00:25:59,700 --> 00:26:02,641
Get those with serious
injuries out of here first.

364
00:26:02,740 --> 00:26:04,697
We've seen enough suffering for today,

365
00:26:04,780 --> 00:26:09,817
and I won't lose any more
men and thus what would later

366
00:26:09,900 --> 00:26:13,397
be known as the war of the
best ended in Marine Ford,

367
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:17,257
the most fearsome battle since the
beginning of the great pirate era,

368
00:26:17,340 --> 00:26:23,780
brought victories and defeats alike,
leaving the world uncertain of its future?

369
00:26:35,420 --> 00:26:38,220
Thank you.
